  "diagnosis_text": "**Diagnosis:** the inter-switch link **s3\u2013s1 is down**, and s3\u2019s forwarding rules still direct remote-host traffic into that failed link.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `h1 \u2192 h5`: **100% loss**\n- Local connectivity remains healthy:\n  - `h1 \u2192 h2`: succeeds on s3\n  - `h6 \u2192 h5`: succeeds on s5\n- Other off-switch traffic from s3 also fails:\n  - `h1 \u2192 h3` and `h2 \u2192 h5`: **100% loss**\n- Both ends of the configured link are disabled:\n  - **s3 port 1**\n  - **s1 port 2**\n- ONOS no longer lists s3\u2013s1 as an active link.\n- s3\u2019s baseline flows still output traffic for h5\u2019s MAC\u2014and all other remote host MACs\u2014to **port 1**. The h5 rule recorded packets, confirming traffic is hitting this stale path and being blackholed.\n- Alternate physical paths via enabled s3\u2013s2 and s3\u2013s4 links exist, but the installed rules are not using them.\n\n**Fault localisation:** physical/administrative failure on **s3:1 \u2194 s1:2**, compounded by stale/non-rerouted baseline flows on **s3**.\n\n**Next step:** restore that link or update/reinstall the s3 forwarding policy so remote destinations use an active alternate path.",
